     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for IR, and may be what you intended.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. You may also want to check it with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
      }
     ],
